1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

  a) Read, study and audit the source code.
  b) Download, install and use Mnémo, free of charge, for personal, educational
     (students, teachers, schools) and other non-commercial purposes.
  c) Modify a copy of the code for your own personal use, on your own
     computer, without sharing the result.
  d) Fork the repository on GitHub, and only on GitHub, solely in order to
     propose changes back to the author (pull request). Such a fork may not
     be promoted, released or used as a separate product.
  e) Send contributions. By doing so you grant the author a perpetual,
     worldwide, royalty-free right to use, modify and distribute them as part
     of Mnémo, including under a different license.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO, WITHOUT THE AUTHOR'S WRITTEN PERMISSION

  a) Redistribute Mnémo, in whole or in part, in source or binary form,
     modified or not (installers, archives, mirrors, package-manager
     entries, app stores, re-uploads…).
  b) Publish or distribute any modified version, derivative work or
     "alternative version" of Mnémo, or any product built from a substantial
     part of its code, design, texts or icons.
  c) Sell, rent, sublicense, or otherwise make money from Mnémo or from a
     derivative of it, including offering it as a paid or hosted service, or
     bundling it in a paid product.
  d) Remove or alter copyright notices, this license, or the attribution to
     the author.
  e) Use the name "Mnémo", its logo or its icon to name or promote another
     product, or in any way suggesting that it is endorsed by the author.

3. OFFICIAL DISTRIBUTION

  The only official sources of Mnémo are the author's repository
  (https://github.com/kusoooback/mnemo) and its "Releases" page. Anything
  else is unofficial and unauthorized.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

  Mnémo includes third-party components (React, Electron, KaTeX, pdf.js,
  better-sqlite3, node-llama-cpp, fonts…) that remain under their own
